<description>
Draw vertical bars for the colors whose bottom code-row frequency equals the marker count.

Input structure
The grid has a dominant background, one solid full-width separator row, a
single contiguous marker run above the separator, and one non-background
code row below the separator.

Rule
Count the marker pixels above the separator. In the code row, find every
color that appears exactly that many times. For each occurrence of such a
color, fill that column for the same number of cells immediately above the
separator, using the code-row color.

Key insight
The marker run is the histogram target count, and the code row gives both
the colors to test and the columns where matching bars must be drawn.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "bottom code row grouped by color frequency, with a marker run above the separator",
  "transform": "for each code-row pixel whose color occurs marker-run length times, fill a vertical bar of that color upward from the separator for marker-run length cells",
  "symbol_instructions": "marker run length gives both the code-row frequency to select and the bar height"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10
  background: 0 (black)
  layout: |
    row 0:    marker run (contiguous horizontal, starts at col 0, color 8/azure)
    rows 1-5: empty (all background)
    row 6:    full-width separator (solid color 5/gray)
    row 7:    empty (all background)
    row 8:    code row (every cell non-background)
    row 9:    empty (all background)
  marker:
    color: 8 (azure) [observed]
    length: 1-4 (contiguous run starting at col 0)
    row: 0 [observed]
  separator:
    color: 5 (gray), distinct from bg, marker, and all code colors [observed]
    row: 6 [observed]
  code_row:
    row: 8 [observed]
    colors: 2-5 distinct non-bg non-separator colors per row
    each cell is non-background
    at least one color must appear exactly marker_length times
    constraint: marker_length <= separator_row so bars fit above separator
  transform:
    count marker pixels (= N)
    find code-row colors whose frequency == N
    for each such cell, draw a vertical bar of that color N cells tall immediately above the separator
    output is same as input plus these bars (bg cells overwritten)
  output_bars:
    selected_columns: 1-6 columns get bars
    matching_colors: 1-3 distinct colors with frequency == marker_length

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (layout is rigid, constraints are simple)
  steps:
    1. Set grid 10x10 all black, separator row 6 all gray (5).
    2. Pick marker_length N in [1,4].
    3. Place marker of color 8 at row 0, cols 0..N-1.
    4. Choose 2-5 distinct colors (not 0, not 5) for the code row.
    5. Assign frequencies to colors such that at least 1 color has freq == N and total == 10. Ensure no non-matching color accidentally has freq N.
    6. Shuffle the 10 code-row values and place at row 8.
    7. Verify bar target cells (rows 6-N to 5, selected columns) are all background (guaranteed by empty rows 1-5, always true when N<=5).
```
